 summary: [
  ["Plants need sunlight and water", "In Activity 10.1, the plant with sunlight and water (Pot A) grew best, the plant without water (Pot B) may have died, and the plant in the dark (Pot C) grew poorly and turned pale. Plants need both sunlight and water to grow."],
  ["Leaves are food factories", "Plants store food as starch. Starch is made in the broad, flat, green leaves, which contain the green pigment chlorophyll that captures sunlight. The iodine test (blue-black colour) shows starch; the leaf is first boiled and decolourised in alcohol in a water bath so the colour change is easy to see."],
  ["Chlorophyll, sunlight and carbon dioxide", "Bhaskar found starch only in the green patches of a leaf from a sunlit plant, not in the dark. The half-leaf inside a bottle of caustic soda (which absorbs carbon dioxide) made no starch. So sunlight, water, chlorophyll and carbon dioxide are all essential."],
  ["Photosynthesis", "Photosynthesis is the process by which plants make food in the presence of sunlight and chlorophyll: Carbon dioxide + Water → Glucose + Oxygen. Glucose gives instant energy and is later stored as starch. The leaf is the main site; other green parts also photosynthesise. Oxygen is released, as Barkha didi’s bubbles showed."],
  ["Stomata", "Stomata are tiny pores on the surface of leaves, seen in a leaf peel under a microscope. They help in the exchange of carbon dioxide and oxygen during photosynthesis and respiration; water vapour also escapes through them."],
  ["Xylem carries water up", "Roots take up water with dissolved minerals. In Activity 10.7 the red ink climbed the stem to the leaves and flowers through thin tubes called xylem."],
  ["Phloem carries food", "Food made in the leaves is carried to all parts of the plant by another set of tubes, the phloem. Some food is stored in other parts such as seeds and roots (and the potato)."],
  ["Plants respire", "Germinating moong seeds gave out carbon dioxide that turned lime water milky. Respiration: Glucose + Oxygen → Carbon dioxide + Water + Energy. All parts of a plant, green or non-green, respire, and the energy is used for growth."],
  ["Balance in nature", "Photosynthesis uses carbon dioxide and gives out oxygen; respiration uses oxygen and gives out carbon dioxide. Together they keep the gases in the air balanced, as a sealed bottle garden shows."]
 ]
